course: dictionary
lesson: 3197
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Enemy can mean a person who hates you, a country fighting against you in a war, or anything that harms something. In «Anyone who disagrees is an enemy», the enemy is a person in an argument, not a soldier.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Most American tarantulas flick itchy barbed hairs at enemies» tells you that enemies are creatures that might attack, so here an enemy is a threat. Ask yourself: who or what is the enemy, and what is it trying to do?
explain: «The Stranger-man thinks the Chief pretended not to notice me because enemies were hiding in the bushes.» The enemies are people who may harm you. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «people who want to harm us» still makes sense, so you have chosen well.
explain: Word forms matter too. Enemy is the singular and enemies is the plural, meaning more than one. In «joined together against outside enemies», the enemies are groups from outside who must be stood up to together.
fact: An enemy is a person who hates you or wants to harm you, or someone you fight against.
fact: The enemy is the army or country fighting against your side in a war.
fact: An enemy can also be anything that harms something: frost is the enemy of flowers.
fact: Enemy is a noun, and its plural is enemies.
fact: A natural enemy is an animal that hunts another animal, such as a predator and its prey.
exercise: «Anyone who disagrees is an enemy.» In Danylo's story, what kind of enemy is this? | A tarantula | *A person who disagrees with him in an argument | Frost that kills flowers | A soldier in a war
exercise: «Enemies were hiding in the bushes.» What does enemies mean here? | Grandparents visiting | *People who want to harm you | Flowers killed by frost | Friends playing a game
exercise: What is the plural of enemy? | enemys | enemyes | enemi | *enemies
test: In a war, the enemy is the ... | river that floods the town | teacher who marks the test | *army or country fighting against your side | best friend of your side
test: «Frost is the enemy of flowers.» What does enemy mean here? | A kind of bird | A friend who helps plants grow | A person who hates flowers | *Anything that harms something
exam: Which sentence uses enemy to mean a country fighting in a war? | *«The enemy army crossed the river at dawn.» | «Anyone who disagrees is an enemy.» | «Tarantulas flick hairs at enemies.» | «Frost is the enemy of flowers.»
